| The outbox: changes that have not reached the service yet, kept in a line
| and sent one at a time, in order — and kept through no network, a closed
| tab and a reload, so a change made on a train lands when the train does.
|
| An application applies a change to what the reader sees the instant it is
| made, and posts the change here to be *told*. This gene owns the telling:
| the line, one item on its way at a time, the pause that grows when the
| service cannot be reached, the copy in `storage` under the reader's own
| key, and one word about whether what the reader is looking at is safe —
| "saving", "saved", "failed", or "" when there is nothing to say.
|
| **It never sends anything itself.** An item is a plain value — the fields
| of a delta, a message, whatever the application's service takes — and
| the application says how one goes. Two handlers are the application's to
| write, and this gene calls both:
|
|   OutboxOutboxDeliver { item } → Asked { id }   send the item; `id` is the number the
|                                       answer will carry, or 0 when it could
|                                       not even be sent
|   OutboxChanged                       the word or the line changed: draw
|
| and three are the application's to call, from wherever its answers land,
| with the number the answer carries:
|
|   OutboxDelivered { id }    the service took it
|   OutboxRejected { id }     the service refused it — dropped, not retried, since
|                       it will never be taken
|   OutboxUndelivered { id }  it never arrived — kept, and tried again after a pause
|
| Each answers `Handled { mine, more }`: whether the number was the item on
| its way (an application has other exchanges than these), and whether the
| line still has something in it — a fresh read taken between two items
| would show the service without the changes still to be sent, and they
| would flicker off the page and back on.
|
| Plain values, deliberately: `Stringify` drops `_class`, so a particle put
| into storage would come back as its fields alone. An item goes in as
| fields and comes out as fields, and `OutboxDeliver` makes the particle — so the
| line survives a reload with nothing here knowing what an item means.
|
| Every handler here begins with `Outbox`, and so do the application's two,
| because a gene's handlers join the one program-wide table: a name like
| `Rejected` would collide with the first application that has an auth.
|
| Needs three aliases named as every application here names them: `store`
| (storage), `json`, and `clock` (timer).

| Oldest first. `outbox_flight` is the number of the item on its way, 0
| when none is; `outbox_pause` is how long the last retry waited.
outbox_items = []
outbox_flight = 0
outbox_pause = 0

| "", "saving", "saved" or "failed" — whether the last *change* is safe.
| Only what happens to an item here moves it: a read that fails has nothing
| to do with whether a change landed, and must not be allowed to say so.
outbox_state = ""

| Where the line is kept: "outbox:" and whatever the application gives —
| the reader's own name, so two people on one browser never see each
| other's changes. "" until opened, and nothing is kept or sent before then.
outbox_key = ""

| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Opening, posting, sending
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

| Open the line under a key: read back what an earlier session left, and
| start sending it. Called once the application knows who the reader is.
OutboxOpen { key } =>
    if key ∉ String or key = ""
        return Noted
    outbox_key = "outbox:" + key
    emit Get { key = outbox_key } to store get kept
    if kept.value ∈ String and kept.value ≠ ""
        emit Parse { text = kept.value } to json get back
        if back.value ∈ Array
            outbox_items = back.value
    emit Length { value = outbox_items } to core get n
    if n.value > 0
        outbox_state = "saving"
        emit OutboxFlush to this
        emit OutboxChanged to this
    return Noted

| A change to be told. Joins the line and goes when its turn comes.
OutboxPost { item } =>
    outbox_state = "saving"
    outbox_items += [item]
    emit OutboxKeep to this
    emit OutboxFlush to this
    emit OutboxChanged to this
    return Noted

| Send the head of the line, unless one is already on its way. Idempotent
| on purpose: `OutboxPost` asks, a retry asks, a reader pressing "retry now" asks,
| and none of them has to know about the others.
OutboxFlush =>
    if outbox_flight ≠ 0
        return Busy
    emit Length { value = outbox_items } to core get n
    if n.value = 0
        return Empty
    emit OutboxDeliver { item = outbox_items[0] } to this get asked
    if asked.id ∈ Number and asked.id > 0
        outbox_flight = asked.id
        return Flushing
    | Could not even be sent — no network, no session. Kept, and tried again
    | after the pause, the same as an item that went and never arrived.
    outbox_state = "failed"
    emit OutboxLater to this
    emit OutboxChanged to this
    return Flushing

| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| What became of the one on its way
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

OutboxDelivered { id } =>
    if id ∉ Number or id ≠ outbox_flight
        return Handled { mine = false, more = false }
    emit OutboxDone to this get rest
    if rest.more
        emit OutboxFlush to this
        return Handled { mine = true, more = true }
    outbox_state = "saved"
    emit Delay { ms = 2500, then = "OutboxSettled" } to clock
    emit OutboxChanged to this
    return Handled { mine = true, more = false }

OutboxRejected { id } =>
    if id ∉ Number or id ≠ outbox_flight
        return Handled { mine = false, more = false }
    emit OutboxDone to this get rest
    outbox_state = "failed"
    if rest.more, emit OutboxFlush to this
    emit OutboxChanged to this
    return Handled { mine = true, more = rest.more }

OutboxUndelivered { id } =>
    if id ∉ Number or id ≠ outbox_flight
        return Handled { mine = false, more = false }
    outbox_flight = 0
    outbox_state = "failed"
    emit OutboxLater to this
    emit OutboxChanged to this
    return Handled { mine = true, more = true }

| The head of the line is done with, one way or the other.
OutboxDone =>
    outbox_flight = 0
    outbox_pause = 0
    rest = []
    i = 0
    loop item over outbox_items
        if i > 0, rest += [item]
        i = i + 1
    outbox_items = rest
    emit OutboxKeep to this
    emit Length { value = outbox_items } to core get n
    return Rest { more = n.value > 0 }

| Try again after a pause that grows: a service that is down for a minute is
| not helped by being asked every second. Two seconds, then double, then
| fifteen at most.
OutboxLater =>
    outbox_pause = outbox_pause * 2
    if outbox_pause < 2000, outbox_pause = 2000
    if outbox_pause > 15000, outbox_pause = 15000
    emit Delay { ms = outbox_pause, then = "OutboxFlush" } to clock
    return Noted

| "Saved" is worth seeing and not worth keeping, so it goes by itself after
| a moment. Guarded, because another change may have started in that moment
| and that one is not finished.
OutboxSettled =>
    if outbox_state = "saved"
        outbox_state = ""
        emit OutboxChanged to this
    return Noted

| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Kept, and asked about
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

OutboxKeep =>
    if outbox_key = ""
        return Noted
    emit Stringify { value = outbox_items } to json get text
    emit Set { key = outbox_key, value = text.value } to store
    return Noted

| For the handler that draws: the word, and how many are still to go.
Outbox =>
    emit Length { value = outbox_items } to core get n
    return OutboxState { state = outbox_state, waiting = n.value, sending = outbox_flight ≠ 0 }
